Vita (--vita-skip-offscreen-anim=off|on, platform/vita/runtime/visual_skips.hpp): a visual-only
speed-up (the picture may change, the game may not). An actor of a few ambient types (the pond's
fish while no fishing rod is out, birds, frogs) that was culled on its last draw skips its morfs'
model calc (mDoExt_McaMorf, McaMorfSO, McaMorf2 modelCalc) while its execute runs: their logic
reads no joint then (the fish's mouth joint feeds only the rod and splashes). The morf's frame and
state are untouched, so the calc runs again from the morf just before the actor's next draw method,
with the pose that tick would have had. The check is the game-state digest (--vita-state-digest):
the same game, tick for tick, with the skip on and off.

